Executive Summary & Overall Conclusions (What We Learned Overall)
Heavy Reliance on Elite Talent: While 182 players scored in the tournament, 20% of all goals came from just 10 players. Team success was heavily tied to having individual world-class finishers who sustained a high Goals-per-Match (G/M) ratio above 1.50.

Optimal Stadium Utilization: The tournament was a massive commercial success with 6.81M total attendance and a high average of ~65.5K fans per game, proving that host venues operated near peak capacity efficiency.

Attack vs. Defense Balance: Top contenders like France and Argentina maintained success through different styles—France via high-volume multi-player attack (16 goals combined by top pair), and Argentina via defensive solidity (1 goal conceded) paired with efficient finishing.
